<title>UK: DE LA RUE FALLS ON PROFIT TAKING.</title>
<headline>DE LA RUE FALLS ON PROFIT TAKING.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British banknote printer and security products group De La Rue Plc fell on Wednesday as the market sold off last week's gains, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's been a bit of profit taking after a good run last week,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>By 1040 GMT, shares in the company were off 25p at 393-1/2p. Last week the stock hit a high of 442p on Friday, levels not seen since early June.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
